  "_comment": "SUBSTITUTION-GATEWAY framing, card 2026-0230. The 'gateway' turn's content_block_start omits content_block.type entirely (latch class B) — the block therefore opens on its first text_delta and its content_block_stop falls through every branch of the parser's content_block_stop handler, emitting nothing. So the block has NO close event, ever. Bind an instance created with a non-Claude backend row (backend:'ollama') to this scenario: the framing is what a substitution gateway produces, and the identity backend's own CLI never emits it. The turns stop mid-block on purpose — the test drives everything after the arm via inst._handleStdoutLine so nothing depends on subprocess timing."
